-- title:
--   Corollary 2.7 — the volume of the minority set is a supermartingale
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal G$ be a temporal graph with fixed degrees and run the standard voter model with two opinions on $\mathcal G$ from any initial state. Let $S_t$ be the minority set at time $t$ (the opinion class of smaller volume, ties to opinion $0$). Then
--   $$\bigl(\mathrm{Vol}(S_t):t\ge0\bigr)$$
--   is a supermartingale with respect to $(\sigma(\mathcal H_t):t\ge0)$.
--
--   The process is absorbed when $S_t=\emptyset$, so this supermartingale is what the consensus-time analysis drives to zero.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the voter process (ξ_t : t ≥ 0) of Definition 1.2 on some probability space → the path measure voterLaw on ℕ → (V → Fin k), built by Ionescu-Tulcea (Kernel.traj) from the synchronous lazy step kernels of Definition 1.2, started at σ₀; reason: the process is constructed from its definition (paper.md R4); every event and expectation of the paper is one of this law
--   - encoding: filtration σ(H_t) generated by the history H_t = (A_0, …, A_t) → Filtration.piLE t on the path space (σ-algebra of ξ_0, …, ξ_t); reason: for two opinions ξ_s and A_s determine each other, so the σ-algebras coincide
--   - encoding: a sequence of undirected graphs on a common vertex set V(G) with common degree d(v) → T : TemporalGraph V: a Fintype V, G t : SimpleGraph V, and the degree data d with degree_eq and one_le_d; reason: the paper's graphs are plain finite graphs (n vertices, m = ½ ∑ d(v) edges, e_t counts edges); no loop or parallel edge occurs in them, the self-loop of Figure 1 only pictures laziness
-- source:
--   Rocha Avila, Dell, Lapinskas, Temporal Conductance and Bounds on the Voter Model for Dynamic Networks, arXiv:2606.13374 (2 Nov 2026), Corollary 2.7, p.13

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_TemporalVoter_minoritySet

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

namespace TemporalVoter

/-- **Corollary 2.7** (arXiv:2606.13374, version of 2 Nov 2026, p.13): in the standard voter model
with `κ = 2` on a temporal graph with fixed degrees, from any initial state, the volume
`(Vol(S_t) : t ≥ 0)` of the minority set is a supermartingale with respect to `(σ(H_t) : t ≥ 0)`. -/
theorem corollary_2_7 {V : Type} [Fintype V] (T : TemporalGraph V) (σ₀ : V → Fin 2) :
    Supermartingale (fun t ω => T.vol (minoritySet T (ω t)))
      (Filtration.piLE (X := fun _ : ℕ => V → Fin 2)) (voterLaw T 2 σ₀) := by sorry

end TemporalVoter
